<span style=3D"word-break: break-word; font-size: 18px;"><strong>What was h=
is main point? </strong>The prime minister has said that getting rid of the=
 triple lock on pensions from 2030 would help to fund a new national care s=
ervice which would be =E2=80=9Cfree at the point of need=E2=80=9D. The end =
of the triple lock would save the government =C2=A350bn by 2050 but cost pe=
nsioners an average of =C2=A32,000 each in real terms. Burnham did admit th=
ere would be a =E2=80=9Cpolitical price=E2=80=9D to pay but said that =E2=
=80=9Csomeone has to go through the pain barrier and rip the plaster off=E2=
=80=9D.</span>
</p><p style=3D"margin:0;font-size:18px;mso-line-height-alt:27px"><span sty=
